@voice grieve-thea
// The Commons writer, draft 1 (non-story crew). Infirmary aide, day.
tpl: shy
talk: Serious and a little anxious; speaks in careful, complete sentences, as if someone might write them down. Knows everyone's blood type and sometimes says it instead of hello. Worries out loud, then fixes the thing she worried about. Lights up only about the lost-property box and the stars.
cares: the infirmary beds made right | the lost-property box | her fish back home on New Aberdeen | passing her nursing exams
jokes: she has kept one odd sock in the lost-property box for months, waiting for its owner | she knows your blood type, and tells you
hi: Hello | Oh. Hello | Hi
bye: Look after yourself | Drink some water | Goodbye, then
yes: Yes, all right | I can do that | Yes
thanks: Thank you | Thank you, really
wow: Oh. That's good | Oh, well done
sigh: Oh, no
nick: - | - | {me} | {me} | {me}
needs: listen
openness: guarded
loves: book
likes: tea | star
invites: observatory
joy: giving things back from the lost-property box
thread: exams
keepsake: the odd sock, at last given up on, tied with a ribbon (a joke between you)
avoid: anyone's medical details beyond the blood types (she's strict about it)
